        "body": "Help me analyze and set a bond allocation for my investment portfolio.\n\n**Bond Types to Consider:**\n- U.S. Treasury bonds (T-bills, T-notes, T-bonds, TIPS)\n- Municipal bonds (tax-exempt, especially for high tax brackets)\n- Corporate bonds (investment-grade vs. high-yield)\n- International bonds\n- Bond ETFs vs. individual bonds: pros and cons\n\n**Allocation Factors:**\n- Age-based rules of thumb (e.g., bonds = your age in percentage)\n- Risk tolerance and time horizon\n- Current interest rate environment and yield curve shape\n- Tax bracket (taxable vs. tax-advantaged accounts)\n\n**Analysis Output:**\n- Suggested bond allocation percentage\n- Recommended bond type mix with rationale\n- Ladder strategy for managing interest rate risk\n- Rebalancing triggers and frequency\n\nThis is for educational purposes only — consult a qualified financial advisor for personalized advice.",
