        "id": "824AE6B0-8C14-43D5-8A7B-089A6C1935A6",
        "body": "Explain the following {{language:Swift}} code at multiple levels:\n\n```\n{{code}}\n```\n\n**Level 1 — What it does** (1–2 sentences):\nPlain-English summary a non-technical person could understand.\n\n**Level 2 — How it works** (paragraph):\nWalk through the logic, data flow, and key decisions. Explain any design patterns used (e.g., observer, strategy, builder) and why they're appropriate here.\n\n**Level 3 — Line-by-line** (annotated):\nGo through each meaningful section and explain:\n- What it does\n- Why it's done this way vs. alternatives\n- Any edge cases it handles (or misses)\n\n**Potential Issues:**\nFlag any bugs, performance concerns, or maintainability risks you notice.",
