        "id": "838CF978-876F-49A3-8041-4DF111D7DC08",
        "body": "Help me determine the best age to claim Social Security benefits.\n\n**Key Ages:**\n- Age 62: earliest, permanently reduced (~30% less than FRA)\n- FRA (66-67): full benefit based on birth year\n- Age 70: maximum benefit (~8%/year increase after FRA)\n\n**Break-Even Analysis:**\n- Calculate crossover age where delaying beats claiming early\n- Factor in time value of money and investment returns\n- Consider life expectancy and health status\n\n**Spousal Strategies:**\n- Spousal benefit (up to 50% of higher earner's FRA benefit)\n- Survivor benefit considerations\n\n**Tax Implications:**\n- Up to 85% of benefits may be taxable depending on provisional income\n- How other retirement income affects taxation\n\nThis is for educational purposes only — consult a qualified financial advisor for personalized advice.",
