      {
        "id": "384A8536-E97C-4E2D-AC86-6095206045E3",
        "body": "Design a notification UX strategy for {{appType:a productivity app}}.\n\nCover:\n1. **Channel selection** — When to use push, in-app banner, badge, email, or SMS\n2. **Priority tiers** — Critical (immediate), high (soon), low (batched daily digest)\n3. **Content format** — Title under 40 chars, body under 100 chars, actionable CTA\n4. **Grouping** — How to collapse related notifications (e.g. '3 new comments' not 3 separate pushes)\n5. **Permission ask** — Pre-permission screen explaining value before the system prompt\n6. **Preferences** — Granular settings UI letting users control each notification type\n7. **Quiet hours** — Respect Do Not Disturb and time zones\n\nInclude a decision matrix mapping event types to channels and priority tiers.",
        "displayOrder": 0
      }
